WEBVTT


00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:01.440 line:15 align:center
Good morning, everyone.


00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.760 line:15 align:center
Today we are in Centennial Park.


00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:07.200 line:15 align:center
My name is Robin and I'm going
to be your birdwatching guide.


00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:16.880 line:15 align:center
This is the call of the rainbow lorikeet.


00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:19.760 line:15 align:center
You can see their rainbow-like colourful plumage.


00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:24.560 line:15 align:center
Last year, the rainbow lorikeet was
the most common bird to be seen


00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:25.600 line:15 align:center
in New South Wales.


00:00:31.570 --> 00:00:33.730 line:15 align:center
The bird you can hear is a
noisy miner.


00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:37.890 line:15 align:center
They feed on flowers and you can
see a flock among the blossoms over there.



00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:43.850 line:15 align:center
These birds can be rather aggressive and
it's common to see them fighting with other birds.


00:00:50.530 --> 00:00:52.050 line:15 align:center
Here is a kookaburra.


00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:54.850 line:15 align:center
Hopefully we will hear their famous laughter.